    "healthAi": "AI-assisted health document check. Where you upload the pages of your pet's vaccination booklet or other health record to Tailmance, Tailmance may process them with AI-assisted text recognition. You are asked to upload every filled page so that the record can be assessed as a whole. The check compares the dated entries of the document, within the required date ranges, with the vaccinations and the internal and external parasite treatments that apply according to the information you entered in the pet profile (species and date of birth). Other care entries and the breed you entered are not checked. Tailmance does not determine a pet's breed from images and does not examine or diagnose any animal. Where the record is complete, consistent and current, it is marked as “checked and approved” until the first date on which a vaccination or treatment falls due again. Records that are incomplete, unclear, inconsistent or outdated are not approved automatically and may be reviewed by a person. You may supplement the record at any time by uploading further pages. The label “checked and approved” records only that the vaccinations and internal and external parasite treatments shown in the document were found to have been completed within the required date ranges. It is not a statement that the animal is in good health, is not veterinary advice, diagnosis or certification, is not a guarantee of any kind and is not a final, binding or legally valid decision. No veterinarian, clinic or register takes part in or confirms the check. The pages are processed on Tailmance's behalf by a cloud text-recognition provider under a data processing agreement, in that provider's European Union region, and are not used by the provider to train its models. AI can make mistakes and may overlook errors or misread a document, so you are asked to check important information yourself. This notice applies to all information and guidance provided by AI-assisted features. Consult a licensed veterinarian for any health decision and do not delay care because of a result shown in the app.",
